upb runtime vendored from protocolbuffers/protobuf tag v33.1
(matches the protoc / protoc-gen-upb version used to (re)generate
 protobuf/pg_query.upb*.{c,h}; keep these in lockstep on upgrade).

Contents: minimal runtime subset for generated-code serialize/parse
(base, hash, mem, message, mini_descriptor, mini_table, wire) +
third_party/utf8_range. Reflection/JSON/text/lex are intentionally omitted.

The upb/wire/decode_fast/ directory has been REMOVED from this vendored tree:
it is upb's optional fast-path parser, used only when UPB_FASTTABLE is enabled
(Clang/GCC + x86-64/ARM64) and the minitables carry fast-decode entries (ours do
not). It relies on compiler-specific machinery that does not build under MSVC.
decode.c references it only under #if UPB_FASTTABLE, so removing it builds and
links cleanly on all platforms. NOTE: a future re-vendor of upb will reintroduce
this directory -- delete it again (the Makefiles also filter it out as a guard).

LOCAL PATCHES (re-apply on upgrade):
- upb/wire/decode.c, _upb_Decoder_GetDelimitedOp(): decode proto3 `string`
  fields as `bytes` (skip UTF-8 validation). SQL string literals may contain
  arbitrary, non-UTF-8 bytes in some server encodings; the previous protobuf-c
  backend never validated them. Search for "libpg_query local patch".
